     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Wednesday, April 26, 2017 at 12:34:02 PM UTC-4, Lu Zhang wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I\r\n uninstalled the R and reinstall only 64 bit version of R and Rtools, \r\nand installed Rstan from github. and tried your command. Still not work.<br></div></blockquote><br>That is hopefully because what I posted was for the case of 32 bit R. If you are using 64 bit R, then it would be<br><br><pre>cat(<span><span>&#39;</span>Sys.setenv(BINPREF = &quot;C:/Rtools/mingw_64/bin/&quot;)<span>&#39;</span></span>,\r\n    <span>file</span> <span>=</span> file.path(Sys.getenv(<span><span>&quot;</span>HOME<span>&quot;</span></span>), <span><span>&quot;</span>.Rprofile<span>&quot;</span></span>), \r\n    <span>sep</span> <span>=</span> <span><span>&quot;</span><span>\\n</span><span>&quot;</span></span>, <span>append</span> <span>=</span> <span>TRUE</span>)</pre><br>or whatever directory g++ resides in.<br><br></div></blockquote></div>"
